====================================================================================================
Third-party code in this repository
====================================================================================================

swifttn93 is derived from tn93, which is MIT-licensed, so swifttn93 and the rest of this repository are distributed under
the MIT licence above (SPDX: MIT). The copyright and permission notices of the code it includes follow.

1. tn93 v1.1.0 (https://github.com/veg/tn93, commit 076eb0f; Sergei L. Kosakovsky Pond, Steven Weaver and contributors).
   solver/argparse.cpp and solver/argparse.hpp are unchanged copies. solver/refkernel.cpp and solver/refkernel.h are
   verbatim excerpts of src/tn93_shared.cc and src/tn93_shared.h. The JSON, histogram and output statements and the TN93
   formula tail in solver/swifttn93.cpp are transcribed from src/TN93.cpp and src/tn93_shared.cc. tn93's licence is
   reproduced below as it stands upstream, including its copyright line.

2. Arm optimized-routines (https://github.com/ARM-software/optimized-routines; Arm Limited), licensed
   MIT OR Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception and used here under MIT. solver/vlog.h re-implements its natural logarithm for
   AVX-512, and solver/vlog_data.h holds the 274 table values of its math/log_data.c (Ln2hi, Ln2lo, A, B, T). glibc ships
   the same routine, which is why those files name glibc; no glibc source code is included.

Libraries that are linked but not included: solver/build.sh links the system's glibc (LGPL-2.1-or-later), libstdc++ and
libgomp (GPL-3.0-or-later with the GCC Runtime Library Exception) statically into the local binary. This repository
distributes source code only; anyone redistributing a built binary must also meet those licences.

